        "title": "fix(active-memory): use truncateUtf16Safe for log value and search query truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nTwo `.slice(0, N)` truncation sites in active-memory may cut UTF-16 surrogate pairs in half when the log value or search query contains multi-byte characters such as emoji.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extensions/active-memory/index.ts`: replace `singleLine.slice(0, MAX_LOG_VALUE_CHARS)` and `normalized.slice(0, MAX_ACTIVE_MEMORY_SEARCH_QUERY_CHARS)` with `truncateUtf16Safe`.\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal",
